# Incentive Allocation Update
Core contributors are proposing to pause KITE Emissions for HAI minting incentives while we reevaluate the incentive design to better align users with the protocol. The goal is to create a more efficient user experience that streamlines active participation in protocol stability.&#x20;

At the same time, we're proposing to cut the fat and go lean on our liquidity incentives. Going forward, we want to stop incentives on all pools except for the HAI/KITE pool on Velodrome and the HAI/WETH pool on Uniswap. LP incentives will come from our OP grant which should be more than enough to sustain us for the next 6-12 months (depending on market conditions).&#x20;

In regards to HAIwheel, KITE staking will still activate revenue share and a HAI Booster. The booster will increase incentives for haiVELO depositors and HAI/WETH LPs on Uniswap up to 2x. This enables KITE stakers to capture more of the value generated by these initiatives. Revenue includes all protocol surplus in excess of the surplus buffer minimum (e.g. what would typically be auctioned off in surplus auctions) and the DAO's percentage split from haiVELO rewards.&#x20;

The daily rewards update will rollout with KITE staking, enabling stakers, haiVELO depositors, and HAI/WETH LPs to claim their rewards daily. All updates are currently being audited and if everything goes smoothly they should be live this month.&#x20;

Overall, the goal is to decrease sell pressure on KITE during this volatile period, while we improve the incentive design and roll out the 'HAIwheel Effect' updates and a new collateral strategy we've been working on for some time.

# Add haiVELO Collateral
### Overview

The DAO has decided to make haiVELO the next new added collateral. There has been discussion both in the discord and on the forum about it.

[Forum Discussion](https://dao.letsgethai.com/forum/post/hai_drops_lsd_haivelo_edition_p995yu35)

Initially this collateral will use the existing VELO oracle.

We have already deployed an oracle for VELO in an earlier governance proposal.

[VELO Oracle Deployment Proposal](https://www.tally.xyz/gov/hai/proposal/11621961110431490196241043268360733374927038949387955412613586439351506309189)

### Details

Adding a new collateral to the system requires deploying multiple contracts and calling functions on existing ones to initialize the new collateral.

Each collateral has it's own set of parameters that define how it interacts with the rest of the HAI system.

Descriptions of what the parameters represent can be found in the following document.

[HAI New Collateral Parameter Guide](https://hackmd.io/@lets-get-hai/new-collateral-parameters)

The parameters used in the other collaterals can be found in the following document.

[HAI Mainnet Paramters Guide](https://hackmd.io/@lets-get-hai/mainnet-params)

### This proposal will have 9 actions

```
// 0x48414956454c4f00000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000
bytes32 constant HAIVELO = bytes32("HAIVELO");
```

**1.** Deploy a new collateral join for haiVELO in the [Collateral Join Factory](https://optimistic.etherscan.io/address/0xfE7987b1Ee45a8d592B15e8E924d50BFC8536143) \[*Executable Code Function 1*]

```
address OP_HAI_VELO_ADDRESS = 0x70f3713512089736661F928B291d1443C8b1BB6A;

collateralJoinFactory.deployCollateralJoin({_cType: HAIVELO, _collateral: OP_HAI_VELO_ADDRESS});
```

**2.** Initialize new collateral in the [Collateral Auction House Factory](https://optimistic.etherscan.io/address/0x81c5C2DA8C1a74c6077B03aD69ca04b74b94B427). This will deploy a new collateral auction house for VELO. \[*Executable Code Function 2*]

